# Vendored upstream — UniVidX/ IS committed (pinned at 382b9002, see
# auto_clone.UNIVIDX_PINNED_COMMIT). It used to be auto-cloned on first
# use and gitignored, but comfyctl deploys with `rsync --delete`: RND had
# no UniVidX/, so every deploy wiped the destination's clone while leaving
# .git behind, and auto_clone only tested for .git — so it declared the
# tree present and the loader died on `No module named 'src.pipelines'`.
# Vendoring gives rsync a source for these files and removes the
# render-time dependency on GitHub being reachable from every worker.
#
# Trimmed vs a bare clone: upstream's assets/ (12 MB of demo mp4s + a
# teaser png, referenced by nothing) is dropped, and the nested .git is
# stripped so this isn't a repo-in-a-repo. 25 MB -> ~900 KB.
#
# To bump the pin: re-clone at the new commit, strip .git, drop assets/,
# and update UNIVIDX_PINNED_COMMIT.
#
# These two are symlink holders the wrapper creates at load time (they
# point into ComfyUI/models/unividx/) — never track their contents.
UniVidX/models/
UniVidX/checkpoints/

# Local model cache (lives under ComfyUI/models/unividx/ anyway, but if
# anyone symlinks it here, don't track the weights).
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored `models/`
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and silently kept
# upstream's source package UniVidX/src/models/ (the DiT, VAE, T5 and
# ModelManager code) out of the vendored copy. After re-vendoring, run
# `git status --ignored UniVidX/` and check nothing under src/ is listed.
/models/
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Node help markdown — generated from modes.py at import so it can't
# drift out of sync with the modes the nodes actually offer.
web/docs/

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
